codex
The cited reduction contains a genuine sign typo (`2B+3` where the displayed odd subpaths sum to `2B−3`), so I’m not going to build on that brittle formula. A cleaner native family comes directly from the same path-forest characterization: total order \(k^2\), so the \(k\) odd-radius fire balls must exactly tile the path components. I’m testing a fixed-component Track B specialization, because the paper explicitly says that regime is polynomial-time and gives the sharp distinction needed for an honest hardness label.
