codex
One local review found the square-prefix plant was too visually exposed: a component length is immediately a perfect square, so the bare task risks collapsing as soon as a solver tests that obvious cue. I’m strengthening the same native Track B family without changing its checker: components will instead be compositions of whole residue classes of fire-ball radii. The short route remains under 300 operations, but the invariant is no longer advertised by a conspicuous square in the instance. This is a material hardening change, so I’ll rerun every gate afterward.
